WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:04.238
Although the house felt empty and dismal after Mother left,

2
00:00:04.238 --> 00:00:10.630
the girls did their best to remain positive and optimistic about matters, at least most of the time.

3
00:00:10.631 --> 00:00:15.641
"If Aunt March makes one nasty remark to me today, I won’t tolerate it,"

4
00:00:15.642 --> 00:00:21.238
Jo grumbled as her hand automatically reached back to pull her long hair into a bun;

5
00:00:21.239 --> 00:00:26.488
when she remembered it wasn’t there any more, she tugged at her short ends.

6
00:00:26.489 --> 00:00:34.676
"Jo, you must be on your best behavior today since Aunt March may be willing to help Father . . . ," Meg remarked doubtfully.

7
00:00:34.677 --> 00:00:41.352
"Aunt March never has and never will help our family until the day she dies," Jo snorted unkindly.

8
00:00:41.353 --> 00:00:49.455
"Until who dies?" Beth inquired, walking toward her sisters with something steaming wrapped inside a kitchen towel.

9
00:00:49.456 --> 00:00:54.805
Meg glanced sharply at Jo, "Never mind, Beth. What have you got there?"

10
00:00:54.806 --> 00:01:02.484
"I thought you might need these," Beth said shyly, as she unwrapped two round (and slightly burnt) buns.

11
00:01:02.485 --> 00:01:08.145
"I baked them with old flour as Mother does, but they’re not as nice as hers."

12
00:01:08.146 --> 00:01:14.222
Not only did the buns warm their hands, but Beth’s kindness warmed their hearts even more.

13
00:01:14.223 --> 00:01:18.549
"Thank you, darling," said Meg, gently hugging her close.

14
00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:25.741
Meg and Jo left the house and as they were about to turn the corner, they looked back as they always did.

15
00:01:25.742 --> 00:01:32.542
This time, instead of Mother, Beth stood at the window waving at her sisters.

16
00:01:32.543 --> 00:01:38.432
"Sweet girl didn’t forget," Jo said, wiping a tear from her eye.

17
00:01:38.433 --> 00:01:44.258
With lighter hearts and steps, the two March sisters proceeded to make their way to work.

18
00:01:44.259 --> 00:01:51.183
The March sisters promised Mother they would write as often as possible to keep her up-to-date on their lives at home.

19
00:01:51.184 --> 00:01:56.289
For Meg, the best time for her to collect her thoughts was after dinner.

20
00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:58.222
My Dearest Mother,

21
00:01:58.223 --> 00:02:03.487
How happy we were to receive your last letter and to find it containing such good news

22
00:02:03.488 --> 00:02:09.092
that even Laurie shed a tear or two, though he insists something went into his eye.

23
00:02:09.093 --> 00:02:17.956
We are so pleased that Father is recovering from his illness with your support and nursing skills to help him. Please send our love to him.

24
00:02:17.957 --> 00:02:25.099
The girls are behaving beautifully and cooperating with us so that everything is in order and well taken care of.

25
00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:29.995
Last night Amy decided she wanted to join the army when she was old enough

26
00:02:29.996 --> 00:02:37.811
but this morning she changed her mind and said she would be a better help for the community as a teacher or instructor of some sort.

27
00:02:37.812 --> 00:02:46.945
Jo unkindly laughed and the two of them exchanged heated words but they made up immediately and are now back to being friends.

28
00:02:46.946 --> 00:02:54.285
Beth hasn’t been practicing the piano as often or as regularly because she feels that more important matters need her attention

29
00:02:54.286 --> 00:03:01.208
and it would be disloyal of her to do what she wants when everyone else is making personal sacrifices.

30
00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:05.681
We told her that you and Father both would want her to spend time for herself,

31
00:03:05.682 --> 00:03:13.087
but Beth feels that as long as you are away she must take on extra duties to make sure everything runs right.

32
00:03:13.088 --> 00:03:19.903
Dearest Mother, we are so grateful to Mr. Brookes, who has been a great strength to you during this time.

33
00:03:19.904 --> 00:03:26.559
Please extend our greetings and best wishes to him as well and tell him that we are eternally in his debt.

34
00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:30.696
We love you very much and anxiously await your return.

35
00:03:30.697 --> 00:03:33.951
Your loving daughter, Meg

36
00:03:33.952 --> 00:03:41.426
Since Jo was accustomed to waking early to write, she used that time to compose letters to Mother instead.

37
00:03:41.427 --> 00:03:43.613
To My Precious Mother,

38
00:03:43.614 --> 00:03:50.744
I always knew Father was a brave fighter and each day he will grow stronger and healthier with your support and love.

39
00:03:50.745 --> 00:03:57.145
We are very lonely without you, Mother, but I must say, the girls have been perfect angels.

40
00:03:57.146 --> 00:04:03.860
Meg watches over us like a mother hen (that’s her new nickname, though I don’t think she cares for it much),

41
00:04:03.861 --> 00:04:08.935
so Beth, Amy, and I, like meek chicks, obey her every word.

42
00:04:08.936 --> 00:04:14.945
Yesterday I nearly ended my friendship with Laurie because basically he called me a liar

43
00:04:14.946 --> 00:04:19.269
(though he didn’t use those words exactly, it was what he implied).

44
00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:24.134
He said I agreed to go somewhere with him and I told him I did no such thing.

45
00:04:24.135 --> 00:04:28.614
Then we said some harsh words to each other and stomped off angrily.

46
00:04:28.615 --> 00:04:38.067
Then I remembered what you said about controlling my temper and I felt bad so I decided to apologize to Laurie, even though I still think I am right.

47
00:04:38.068 --> 00:04:43.045
But there he was, standing in front of our door, looking like a lost puppy.

48
00:04:43.046 --> 00:04:47.058
We both said sorry and are now best friends once again.

49
00:04:47.059 --> 00:04:51.275
I’m getting accustomed to my new hair and others seem to be as well.

50
00:04:51.276 --> 00:04:57.309
I even heard old Mrs. Kemper say that the boyish cut suits me and I took it as a compliment.

51
00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:00.683
Give my love to Father and greetings to Mr. Brookes.

52
00:05:00.684 --> 00:05:04.125
All my love to you, Mother, until I write again.

53
00:05:04.126 --> 00:05:07.645
Yours forever, Jo

54
00:05:07.646 --> 00:05:15.855
The two younger sisters wrote their letters whenever they felt like it, so theirs were shorter and more frequent than Meg’s and Jo’s.

55
00:05:15.856 --> 00:05:17.467
Dear Mother,

56
00:05:17.468 --> 00:05:24.033
I am sending some pressed pansies from the garden, as I am hoping that it will remind Father of home.

57
00:05:24.034 --> 00:05:32.570
I have also included a short note from the Hummels, though I wrote down what Mrs. Hummel said since her English is still quite poor.

58
00:05:32.571 --> 00:05:37.591
The children all seem to be well. They miss you almost as much as I do.

59
00:05:37.592 --> 00:05:40.277
Please give Father a kiss from his Beth.

60
00:05:40.278 --> 00:05:44.626
I love you, Mother dearest. Little Beth

61
00:05:44.627 --> 00:05:50.917
My Loving Mother, You will be happy to know that I am doing my lessons faithfully.

62
00:05:50.918 --> 00:05:57.819
Jo was so cross with me the other day because I forgot (I really did) to write my essay.

63
00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:03.015
But today she seemed pleased with what I showed her. I’m back with oils now.

64
00:06:03.016 --> 00:06:08.967
I find that clay doesn’t allow me to express my emotions as clearly as oils do.

65
00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:12.982
I’ve inserted a picture I completed just this morning.

66
00:06:12.983 --> 00:06:16.293
Please tell Father it is drawn with love.

67
00:06:16.294 --> 00:06:19.647
I am thinking about cutting my hair like Jo’s.

68
00:06:19.648 --> 00:06:27.300
I rather like that carefree style and feel that it would go well with my natural curls. What do you think, Mother?

69
00:06:27.301 --> 00:06:33.341
Mr. Laurence visits us daily and every other day we are invited to dine at the mansion.

70
00:06:33.342 --> 00:06:41.300
His cook has excellent taste and prepares for us cuisine from the continent (which is Europe, in case you didn’t know).

71
00:06:41.301 --> 00:06:44.904
Just the other day she prepared a French meal for us.

72
00:06:44.905 --> 00:06:51.471
Mother, it was heaven. One day I must go over and learn her art.

73
00:06:51.472 --> 00:06:53.958
Oh, it sounds like Jo is back home.

74
00:06:53.959 --> 00:06:57.330
I’d better get back to my lessons or else . . .

75
00:06:57.331 --> 00:06:59.692
Please give my love to Father.

76
00:06:59.693 --> 00:07:02.420
Affectionately, Amy

77
00:07:02.421 --> 00:07:06.948
Whenever or wherever the girls wrote their letters was up to them.

78
00:07:06.949 --> 00:07:15.530
When they received a letter from Mother, however, the sisters gathered closely together to listen and find comfort in Mother’s loving words,

79
00:07:15.531 --> 00:07:21.347
which helped them to have hope, joy, and faith for the future.

